      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Actually, there was a significant error in my previous response regarding \"estrogen synthesis,\" as ACE inhibitors do not affect estrogen levels, and that concept is likely a hallucination. Angiotensin II normally stimulates the adrenal cortex to release aldosterone, so when ACE inhibitors block angiotensin II, they simply prevent this stimulation, lowering aldosterone release. Lower aldosterone means the kidneys dump more sodium and water into your urine rather than reabsorbing them. Focus on this blockade of signaling rather than hormonal side effects like estrogen for your exam preparation.",
